{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NiaqYu4Ncb8pc14428JzJi","type":"tool_result","content":"522\t}\n523\t\n524\t/// Replace the PN-encryption header-protection key in `pn_enc_slot`\n525\t/// with a key freshly derived from `secret` using HKDF-Expand-Label\n526\t/// with the HP label and `prefix_label`.  Any previously installed\n527\t/// key is dropped.  `suite` and `is_enc` are present for API parity\n528\t/// with the C signature; only the secret and prefix label affect the\n529\t/// derivation in the current AES-128-GCM-only build.\n530\t/// C: `picoquic_set_pn_enc_from_secret` (tls_api.c:1311-1330).\n531\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n532\tfn set_pn_enc_from_secret(\n533\t    pn_enc_slot: &mut Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>>,\n534\t    _suite: AeadSuiteId,\n535\t    _is_enc: bool,\n536\t    secret: &[u8],\n537\t    prefix_label: &str,\n538\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n539\t    *pn_enc_slot = Some(header_key_from_secret(secret, prefix_label)?);\n540\t    Ok(())\n541\t}\n542\t\n543\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n544\t// Hash context — wraps the per-algorithm hash state for the\n545\t// `hash_update` / `hash_finalize` pair.\n546\t\n547\t/// An in-progress hash computation.  Replaces the opaque\n548\t/// `ptls_hash_context_t *` used by the C `picoquic_hash_update` /\n549\t/// `picoquic_hash_finalize` API.  Create with\n550\t/// `HashContext::new(algorithm_name)`.\n551\t/// C: `void * picoquic_hash_create(const char *algorithm_name)`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b264549-cec3-4800-9d6a-f061bc9f44d5","uuid":"b1745f6b-65c2-4e31-9384-f68e15247c46","timestamp":"2026-05-07T10:07:38.522Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tls_api.rs","content":"}\n\n/// Replace the PN-encryption header-protection key in `pn_enc_slot`\n/// with a key freshly derived from `secret` using HKDF-Expand-Label\n/// with the HP label and `prefix_label`.  Any previously installed\n/// key is dropped.  `suite` and `is_enc` are present for API parity\n/// with the C signature; only the secret and prefix label affect the\n/// derivation in the current AES-128-GCM-only build.\n/// C: `picoquic_set_pn_enc_from_secret` (tls_api.c:1311-1330).\n#[allow(dead_code)]\nfn set_pn_enc_from_secret(\n    pn_enc_slot: &mut Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>>,\n    _suite: AeadSuiteId,\n    _is_enc: bool,\n    secret: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    *pn_enc_slot = Some(header_key_from_secret(secret, prefix_label)?);\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Hash context — wraps the per-algorithm hash state for the\n// `hash_update` / `hash_finalize` pair.\n\n/// An in-progress hash computation.  Replaces the opaque\n/// `ptls_hash_context_t *` used by the C `picoquic_hash_update` /\n/// `picoquic_hash_finalize` API.  Create with\n/// `HashContext::new(algorithm_name)`.\n/// C: `void * picoquic_hash_create(const char *algorithm_name)`.","numLines":30,"startLine":522,"totalLines":2257}}}
